# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum-HPC integration challenge {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"
msgstr "Tantangan integrasi kuantum-HPC {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-performance computing (HPC) workflows often require seamless coordination between classical compute clusters and quantum processing units (QPUs). Different quantum hardware backends and services expose distinct authentication mechanisms, wire formats, and job lifecycle APIs. Integrating IBM Quantum systems into HPC workload managers (such as Slurm) requires a clean, standard interface for resource acquisition, job execution, and session management.\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja high-performance computing (HPC) sering membutuhkan koordinasi yang mulus antara klaster komputasi klasik dan quantum processing unit (QPU). Backend dan layanan hardware quantum yang berbeda mengekspos mekanisme autentikasi, format wire, dan API siklus hidup job yang berbeda-beda. Mengintegrasikan sistem IBM Quantum ke dalam workload manager HPC (seperti Slurm) membutuhkan antarmuka yang bersih dan standar untuk akuisisi resource, eksekusi job, dan manajemen session.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What QRMI is {#what-qrmi-is}"
msgstr "Apa itu QRMI {#what-qrmi-is}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** is a middleware library written in Rust that standardizes access to quantum hardware from HPC schedulers and classical applications. It exposes a single unified lifecycle API:\n"
msgstr "**Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** adalah library middleware yang ditulis dalam Rust yang menstandardisasi akses ke hardware quantum dari scheduler HPC dan aplikasi klasik. Ia mengekspos satu API siklus hidup yang terpadu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QRMI is published as an open-source project at [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) and is described in the overview paper [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"
msgstr "QRMI dipublikasikan sebagai proyek open-source di [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) dan dijelaskan dalam paper overview [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key design choices {#key-design-choices}"
msgstr "Pilihan desain utama {#key-design-choices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Resource lifecycle, not circuit compilation.** QRMI handles the acquire/submit/poll/release lifecycle and nothing else. Circuit compilation, optimization, and transpilation remain in the application layer (for example, Qiskit). This keeps the interface minimal and composable.\n"
msgstr "**Siklus hidup resource, bukan kompilasi circuit.** QRMI menangani siklus hidup acquire/submit/poll/release dan tidak ada lagi selain itu. Kompilasi circuit, optimisasi, dan transpilasi tetap berada di layer aplikasi (misalnya, Qiskit). Ini menjaga antarmuka tetap minimal dan dapat dikomposisi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vendor portability model.** While QRMI provides common job-management calls (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) across supported hardware backends, changing vendors also requires different compilation passes, vendor-specific payload construction, and result decoding in the application layer.\n"
msgstr "**Model portabilitas vendor.** Meskipun QRMI menyediakan panggilan manajemen job umum (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) di berbagai backend hardware yang didukung, mengganti vendor juga membutuhkan pass kompilasi yang berbeda, konstruksi payload spesifik vendor, dan decoding hasil di layer aplikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Native IBM payload format.** For IBM Quantum backends, QRMI uses OpenQASM 3 JSON payloads (`QiskitPrimitive`) conforming to the Qiskit Runtime schema.\n"
msgstr "**Format payload native IBM.** Untuk backend IBM Quantum, QRMI menggunakan payload JSON OpenQASM 3 (`QiskitPrimitive`) yang sesuai dengan skema Qiskit Runtime.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Configuration through environment variables.** Credentials and endpoint URLs are read from environment variables at runtime. In an HPC cluster, the Slurm QRMI SPANK plugin sets these automatically when a job is dispatched. In a notebook or interactive session, you load them from a `.env` file. Application code never contains hardcoded credentials or endpoint URLs.\n"
msgstr "**Konfigurasi melalui variabel lingkungan.** Kredensial dan URL endpoint dibaca dari variabel lingkungan saat runtime. Di klaster HPC, plugin SPANK Slurm QRMI mengatur ini secara otomatis saat job dikirim. Di notebook atau session interaktif, Anda memuatnya dari file `.env`. Kode aplikasi tidak pernah berisi kredensial atau URL endpoint yang di-hardcode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**HPC scheduler integration through GRES.** When a Slurm job requests quantum resources using the QRMI SPANK plugin interface (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` and `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), the plugin injects `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` and `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` into the job environment. Applications call `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` to discover which resources were allocated &mdash; no hardcoded backend names required. `QRMIService` wraps this pattern for Qiskit users.\n"
msgstr "**Integrasi scheduler HPC melalui GRES.** Ketika job Slurm meminta resource quantum menggunakan antarmuka plugin SPANK QRMI (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` dan `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), plugin menyisipkan `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` dan `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` ke dalam lingkungan job. Aplikasi memanggil `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` untuk menemukan resource mana yang dialokasikan &mdash; tidak perlu nama backend yang di-hardcode. `QRMIService` membungkus pola ini untuk pengguna Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The core API calls {#the-core-api-calls}"
msgstr "Panggilan API inti {#the-core-api-calls}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call | Purpose |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Acquire access to the resource (for example, opens a dedicated session); returns a lock token |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Retrieve backend capabilities (qubits, gates, coupling map) as JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Submit a quantum job; returns a job ID |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Poll job status (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Retrieve completed job results as a raw JSON string |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Cancel or clean up a job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Release the resource lock (for example, closes the session) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Panggilan | Tujuan |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Mengakuisisi akses ke resource (misalnya, membuka session khusus); mengembalikan token lock |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Mengambil kapabilitas backend (qubit, gate, coupling map) sebagai JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Mengirimkan job quantum; mengembalikan ID job |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Melakukan poll status job (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Mengambil hasil job yang selesai sebagai string JSON mentah |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Membatalkan atau membersihkan job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Melepaskan lock resource (misalnya, menutup session) |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this tutorial covers {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"
msgstr "Yang dibahas tutorial ini {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is structured in two parts:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini terstruktur dalam dua bagian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Steps 1–3 (small-scale examples):** Introduce the QRMI API with a simple Bell state circuit demonstration on IBM Quantum hardware, covering direct low-level primitive usage as well as high-level `QRMIService` and `SamplerV2` integration.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1–3 (contoh skala kecil):** Memperkenalkan API QRMI dengan demonstrasi circuit Bell state sederhana pada hardware IBM Quantum, mencakup penggunaan primitive tingkat rendah secara langsung serta integrasi `QRMIService` dan `SamplerV2` tingkat tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Large-scale hardware example:** A complete SQD workflow for the N$_2$ molecule at a bond distance of 1.0 $\\AA$ (cc-pVDZ basis active space, 26 spatial orbitals / 52 qubits), executed on IBM Quantum hardware through QRMI. SQD combines quantum sampling of a LUCJ ansatz constructed with `ffsim` and self-consistent configuration recovery with `qiskit-addon-sqd`.\n"
msgstr "**Contoh hardware skala besar:** Alur kerja SQD lengkap untuk molekul N$_2$ pada jarak ikatan 1,0 $\\AA$ (active space basis cc-pVDZ, 26 orbital spasial / 52 qubit), dijalankan pada hardware IBM Quantum melalui QRMI. SQD menggabungkan sampling quantum dari ansatz LUCJ yang dibangun dengan `ffsim` dan pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent dengan `qiskit-addon-sqd`.\n"

