# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale examples {#small-scale-examples}"
msgstr "Contoh skala kecil {#small-scale-examples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–3 introduce the QRMI API by using simple circuits. Each step maps to a core phase of the QRMI lifecycle against IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Langkah 1–3 memperkenalkan API QRMI dengan menggunakan circuit sederhana. Setiap langkah memetakan ke fase inti dari siklus hidup QRMI terhadap hardware IBM Quantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payload for these initial steps is a small Bell state circuit chosen to be fast and inexpensive to run.\n"
msgstr "Payload untuk langkah-langkah awal ini adalah circuit Bell state kecil yang dipilih agar cepat dan murah untuk dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These examples use hardware because they demonstrate remote resource allocation and job management. A local circuit simulator does not validate the QRMI service and scheduler integration. Running this notebook submits IBM Quantum jobs and requires access to the configured backend.\n"
msgstr "Contoh-contoh ini menggunakan hardware karena mendemonstrasikan alokasi resource jarak jauh dan manajemen job. Simulator circuit lokal tidak memvalidasi layanan QRMI dan integrasi scheduler. Menjalankan notebook ini mengirimkan job IBM Quantum dan membutuhkan akses ke backend yang dikonfigurasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map the classical problem to a quantum resource {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Memetakan masalah klasik ke resource quantum {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first step in any QRMI workflow is to create a `QuantumResource` object and verify that it is accessible.\n"
msgstr "Langkah pertama dalam alur kerja QRMI apa pun adalah membuat objek `QuantumResource` dan memverifikasi bahwa itu dapat diakses.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_target()` retrieves the backend's hardware description (qubit count, basis gates, coupling map) and packages it as a Qiskit `Target` object, which the transpiler uses in Step 2.\n"
msgstr "`get_target()` mengambil deskripsi hardware backend (jumlah qubit, basis gate, coupling map) dan mengemasnya sebagai objek `Target` Qiskit, yang digunakan transpiler pada Langkah 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Mengoptimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi hardware quantum {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before submission, use Qiskit to transpile the circuit to the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA), using the `Target` object retrieved in Step 1.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum pengiriman, gunakan Qiskit untuk mentranspilasi circuit ke instruction set architecture (ISA) backend, menggunakan objek `Target` yang diambil pada Langkah 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example then builds a `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, which wraps the OpenQASM 3 circuit string and job metadata into the IBM primitive schema.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini kemudian membangun `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, yang membungkus string circuit OpenQASM 3 dan metadata job ke dalam skema primitive IBM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using QRMI primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Mengeksekusi menggunakan primitive QRMI {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the payload built, the example submits the job and polls for completion. `task_start()` returns a job ID immediately; `task_status()` is polled until the status is no longer `Queued`/`Running`. Results are retrieved as a raw JSON string and parsed to extract measurement samples.\n"
msgstr "Dengan payload yang sudah dibangun, contoh ini mengirimkan job dan melakukan poll hingga selesai. `task_start()` langsung mengembalikan ID job; `task_status()` di-poll hingga statusnya bukan lagi `Queued`/`Running`. Hasil diambil sebagai string JSON mentah dan diparsing untuk mengekstrak sampel pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell keeps acquisition, execution, and cleanup together so that failures after acquisition still release a notebook-owned session.\n"
msgstr "Sel berikut menyatukan akuisisi, eksekusi, dan pembersihan sehingga kegagalan setelah akuisisi tetap melepaskan session milik notebook.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Higher-level Qiskit interface: QRMIService and SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"
msgstr "Antarmuka Qiskit tingkat lebih tinggi: QRMIService dan SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The raw lifecycle above provides explicit control over every call. For standard Qiskit workflows, QRMI provides a `SamplerV2` primitive implementing `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"
msgstr "Siklus hidup mentah di atas menyediakan kontrol eksplisit atas setiap panggilan. Untuk alur kerja Qiskit standar, QRMI menyediakan primitive `SamplerV2` yang mengimplementasikan `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Lifecycle management\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Manajemen siklus hidup\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`SamplerV2` handles payload serialization, submission (`task_start`), polling, and result decoding. In an HPC batch setting (for example, with Slurm), allocation and release are managed by the scheduler and the SPANK plugin. In an interactive Python session using direct low-level API objects, `acquire()` and `release()` can be used to explicitly manage dedicated sessions.\n"
msgstr "`SamplerV2` menangani serialisasi payload, pengiriman (`task_start`), polling, dan decoding hasil. Dalam pengaturan batch HPC (misalnya, dengan Slurm), alokasi dan pelepasan dikelola oleh scheduler dan plugin SPANK. Dalam session Python interaktif menggunakan objek API tingkat rendah secara langsung, `acquire()` dan `release()` dapat digunakan untuk mengelola session khusus secara eksplisit.\n"

